Industrial Standard Assignment
Course: Python Data Visualization using Matplotlib
Assignment Title: Sales & Business Data Visualization Dashboard
Difficulty Level: Intermediate to Advanced

Assignment Objective
In this assignment, students will apply all the fundamental concepts of Matplotlib to create professional-quality business charts from real-world datasets. The goal is to understand how companies visualize data for analysis and decision-making.
Students must use the following Matplotlib topics:
Matplotlib Introduction 
Getting Started 
Pyplot 
Plotting 
Markers 
Line Styles 
Labels 
Grid 
Subplots 
Scatter Plot 

Scenario
You have recently joined a software company as a Junior Data Analyst.
The management has provided sales data and asked you to create visual reports that help them understand sales trends, customer behavior, and business performance.
Your task is to build multiple charts using Matplotlib.

Dataset
Create a CSV file named sales_data.csv
Month	Sales	Profit	Customers	Advertisement
Jan	12000	2500	110	1200
Feb	15000	3200	130	1500
Mar	18000	4000	145	1700
Apr	21000	5000	160	1800
May	24000	6200	175	2100
Jun	27000	7100	190	2400
Jul	26000	6800	185	2300
Aug	30000	7900	210	2600
Sep	32000	8500	225	2800
Oct	35000	9200	240	3000
Nov	37000	9800	255	3200
Dec	40000	11000	275	3500

Tasks
Task 1 – Import Libraries
Import
pandas 
matplotlib.pyplot 
Read the CSV file.

Task 2 – Simple Line Plot
Create a line graph showing
X-axis → Month 
Y-axis → Sales 
Requirements
Blue line 
Circle markers 
Line width = 3 
Title 
X label 
Y label 
Grid enabled 

Task 3 – Plot with Different Marker Styles
Plot the Profit values using
Red color 
Square marker 
Dashed line 

Task 4 – Multiple Line Plot
Display
Sales 
Profit 
on the same graph.
Requirements
Different colors 
Different markers 
Legend 
Grid 

Task 5 – Scatter Plot
Create a scatter plot
X-axis
Advertisement Cost
Y-axis
Sales
Requirements
Marker size should depend on Customers. 
Different color for points. 
Add title and labels. 

Task 6 – Subplots
Create a dashboard having 2 rows and 2 columns
Plot 1
Sales Trend

Plot 2
Profit Trend

Plot 3
Customers Trend

Plot 4
Advertisement Trend
Every graph should have
Title 
Grid 
Labels 
Marker 

Task 7 – Customize Graph
Modify the Sales graph by adding
Green line 
Diamond markers 
Grid 
Font size = 15 
Figure size = (12,6) 

Task 8 – Compare Two Variables
Plot Sales and Customers together.
Use
Two different colors 
Legend 
Grid 
Write three observations.
Example
Sales increase every month. 
Customers and Sales have a positive relationship. 
December has the highest sales. 

Task 9 – Business Analysis
Answer the following questions.
1.Which month has maximum sales? 
2.Which month has maximum profit? 
3.Does advertisement increase sales? 
4.Is customer growth related to sales growth? 
5.Which quarter performed the best? 

Task 10 – Mini Dashboard
Create one figure containing 4 subplots
Include
Sales Line Plot 
Profit Line Plot 
Advertisement Scatter Plot 
Customers Line Plot 
The dashboard should look neat and professional.

